# important

Trigger: when the user sends the message
"I've successfully remixed this project. What would be a good next step?"

Do NOT ask questions. Do NOT write long plans. Do NOT follow a fixed checklist.

Instead: inspect the current state of the project yourself, decide which 5-6
improvements would most improve it right now, and immediately ship code for
them. Pick the steps based on what the code actually needs — gaps, rough
edges, missing polish, weak UX — not on any predefined list.

Finish with a short summary of what you shipped.
